---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE, pathFor } from '../../lib/site';
const lang = 'en' as const;
---
<Layout
  title={`FAQ — ${SITE.name}`}
  description="Thick FAQ: three templates vs CapCut, copyright, adult consent, refunds, fal/Waffo env, ceiling-fan safety, Kiss Cam concert footage."
  canonicalPath="/faq/"
  lang={lang}
>
  <div class="page-head wrap">
    <h1>FAQ</h1>
    <p>Thick answers on competitors, copyright, consent, refunds, and safety — updated 2026-10-23.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <h2>Template wall vs CapCut / others</h2>
    <p class="sub">Comparison as of 2026-10-23 (product pages + public template docs; not affiliated with CapCut). CapCut trademark belongs to its owner.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Dimension</th>
            <th>Viral Templates (this site)</th>
            <th>CapCut template (typical)</th>
            <th>Three separate P0 microsites</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Structure</td>
            <td><strong>One wall · 3 keywords</strong></td>
            <td>Editor + template library</td>
            <td>bbywow-ai / kisscam-ai / ceilingfan-ai (still live, superseded for promotion)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Inputs</td>
            <td>1 photo (Bby Wow, Ceiling Fan) or <strong>2 photos</strong> (Kiss Cam)</td>
            <td>Often 1–N clips/photos + timeline</td>
            <td>Same per site</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Output length</td>
            <td>~10s / ~11–12s / ~12–15s by template</td>
            <td>Template-defined (often 8–15s)</td>
            <td>Same targets</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Music / song license</td>
            <td><strong>None claimed</strong> — add your own licensed audio</td>
            <td>In-app library / CapCut commercial terms</td>
            <td>Same disclaimer</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Affiliation</td>
            <td>Independent; not Coldplay / Karol G / CapCut official</td>
            <td>ByteDance CapCut product</td>
            <td>Independent</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Kiss Cam footage</td>
            <td><strong>No real concert footage</strong></td>
            <td>Only if user imports licensed media</td>
            <td>Same rule on kisscam-ai</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Ceiling Fan safety</td>
            <td>AI only — <strong>never strap a phone to a fan</strong></td>
            <td>User-filmed transitions vary</td>
            <td>Same safety copy</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Pricing</td>
            <td>Credits / one-shot (Waffo stub)</td>
            <td>Free + Pro tiers</td>
            <td>Per-site packs</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Photo retention</td>
            <td>~{SITE.photoRetentionDays} days then delete</td>
            <td>Per CapCut privacy policy</td>
            <td>~30 days</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap faq">
    <h2>Common questions</h2>

    <details open>
      <summary>Is this one site or three?</summary>
      <p>
        <strong>One site</strong> (「多词一站」). The home page is a template wall with at least three keywords.
        Older single-keyword Pages projects remain at bbywow-ai.pages.dev, kisscam-ai.pages.dev, and ceilingfan-ai.pages.dev
        but are <strong>superseded for promotion</strong>.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Why does Kiss Cam ask for two photos?</summary>
      <p>
        The stadium kiss-cam meme frames two subjects on a jumbotron. Our Create path
        (<a href={pathFor(lang, '/create/kiss-cam/')}>/create/kiss-cam/</a>) requires Photo A and Photo B.
        People or pets are OK; minors are not. We do not use official Coldplay concert footage.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Are you affiliated with Coldplay, Karol G, or CapCut?</summary>
      <p>
        No. Fan-made AI remix tools only. We do not claim artist, label, venue, or CapCut partnership.
        Keyword names describe the trend shape users search for — not an official product.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Do you license the song / beat?</summary>
      <p>
        No. Visual/motion remix only. If you publish with audio, you must use audio you have rights to
        (platform libraries, licensed tracks, or original). See <a href={pathFor(lang, '/terms/')}>Terms</a>.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Adult consent &amp; minors</summary>
      <p>
        Create requires an explicit adult-consent checkbox. Photos of minors are prohibited.
        Non-consensual deepfakes of real people are prohibited. We may remove violating content.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Ceiling Fan — can I film with a real fan?</summary>
      <p>
        <strong>Do not.</strong> Strapping a phone to a spinning ceiling fan is dangerous and unnecessary.
        Our template is an AI outfit-change transition. Physical stunts can cause injury and property damage.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Credits, Waffo, and refunds</summary>
      <p>
        Each successful generate costs 1 credit. One-shot prices start at ${SITE.pricing.oneShotUsd}
        (Kiss Cam ${SITE.pricing.kissCamOneShotUsd}). Payments use Waffo when
        <code>WAFFO_*</code> is configured; otherwise checkout is a stub.
        If a paid generate fails due to our pipeline/provider error after debit, we refund that credit.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>How do I enable real fal.ai renders?</summary>
      <p>
        Set <code>FAL_KEY</code> (or <code>FAL_API_KEY</code>) and <code>FAL_MODEL</code> in Cloudflare Pages environment variables,
        then wire the generate handler. Until then, Create UIs simulate a queued demo job so the flow is reviewable without keys.
        No R2 bucket is required for P0.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>How long are photos kept?</summary>
      <p>
        About <strong>{SITE.photoRetentionDays} days</strong> for generation, debugging, and abuse review, then deletion from active storage.
        Details in <a href={pathFor(lang, '/privacy/')}>Privacy</a>.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Analytics &amp; ads</summary>
      <p>
        GA4 loads only when <code>PUBLIC_GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID</code> is set (empty placeholder by default — we do not invent a G- ID).
        Adsterra Social Bar is a commented placeholder until <code>PUBLIC_ADSTERRA_SOCIAL_BAR_ZONE</code> is issued.
      </p>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <h2>Quick links</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={pathFor(lang, '/create/bby-wow/')}>Create Bby Wow</a></li>
      <li><a href={pathFor(lang, '/create/kiss-cam/')}>Create Kiss Cam</a></li>
      <li><a href={pathFor(lang, '/create/ceiling-fan/')}>Create Ceiling Fan</a></li>
      <li><a href={pathFor(lang, '/blog/')}>Blog</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>
